//
// Four properties per code point, because several UAX #14 rules are written in
// terms of things other than Line_Break:
//   Line_Break            LineBreak.txt
//   East_Asian_Width      EastAsianWidth.txt         (LB19a, LB30)
//   General_Category      DerivedGeneralCategory.txt (LB15a/b, LB30b, LB1)
//   Extended_Pictographic emoji-data.txt             (LB30b)
//
// LB1's resolution is applied HERE, not at run time: AI/SG/XX become AL, CJ
// becomes NS, and SA becomes CM when its general category is Mn or Mc and AL
// otherwise. Those are the choices the UCD's own LineBreakTest.txt assumes. CB is
// deliberately left alone, because LB20 is written in terms of it. Resolving in
// the generator lets the rules read the way the standard writes them.
//
// 2175 ranges, fifteen characters each: six start, six end, two class,
// one flags. AL with no flags is the unstored default. Binary searched over a
// fixed-width hexadecimal literal — NUL-free, because a str is strlen-based on
// the LLVM backend.
